---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy Policy | Bright School"
  description="How Bright School collects, uses and protects the information parents give us about themselves and their children."
>
  <section class="wrap page-head">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="small">Last updated: 11 November 2026</p>
  </section>
  <section class="wrap section" style="padding-bottom: var(--section)">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>Bright School teaches live online coding and AI classes to children aged 6 to 15. This page explains what information we collect, why, and what you can ask us to do with it. "We" means Bright School; "you" means the parent or guardian.</p>

      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We collect only what we need to book and teach classes.</li>
        <li>A parent or guardian gives us the information. We do not ask children for it.</li>
        <li>We never sell personal information and we do not use it for advertising by other companies.</li>
        <li>You can ask us to show, correct or delete your information at any time.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>About you:</strong> your name, email address, phone or WhatsApp number, and your time zone.</li>
        <li><strong>About your child:</strong> first name, age, and any coding experience you tell us about.</li>
        <li><strong>About classes:</strong> bookings, attendance, the course your child is taking, the teacher's notes on progress, and the projects your child makes in class.</li>
        <li><strong>Messages:</strong> what you send us by email, WhatsApp or the booking form.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not take card or bank details on this website.</p>

      <h2>Why we use it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To book, confirm and remind you about classes.</li>
        <li>To teach your child at the right level and tell you how they are doing.</li>
        <li>To answer your questions and send you information about courses you asked about.</li>
        <li>To take payment and keep the records we are required to keep.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>If we send you news or offers, every message will tell you how to stop them.</p>

      <h2>Children's information</h2>
      <p>Classes are for children, so we take extra care:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>We only hold a child's information that a parent or guardian has given us.</li>
        <li>We do not publish a child's name, photo or project without the parent's written permission.</li>
        <li>We do not record classes without asking you first.</li>
        <li>Every AI tool is used with a teacher present, and children are not asked to type personal details into AI tools.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
      <p>We share information only with your child's teacher and with the services we use to run the school. Each one receives only what it needs:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Cal.com</strong>, for booking class times.</li>
        <li><strong>Google</strong>, for email and for classes on Google Meet.</li>
        <li><strong>HubSpot</strong>, for keeping track of enquiries and enrolments.</li>
        <li><strong>WhatsApp</strong>, when you choose to message us there.</li>
        <li><strong>Amazon Web Services</strong>, which hosts this website.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>These companies may store information outside the country you live in. We may also share information if the law requires us to.</p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>This website does not use advertising cookies. The booking calendar is provided by Cal.com and may set cookies it needs to work. If we add visitor statistics later, we will update this page first.</p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>We keep your information while your child is learning with us. If you enquired but did not enrol, or your child has stopped, we keep contact details for up to 24 months so we can stay in touch, unless you ask us to delete them sooner. Records of payments are kept for as long as the law requires.</p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>You can ask us at any time to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>show you the information we hold about you and your child;</li>
        <li>correct anything that is wrong;</li>
        <li>delete your information;</li>
        <li>stop sending you news or offers.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We will reply within 30 days.</p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>If we change this policy we will update the date at the top. If the change is significant, we will tell enrolled families directly.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>For anything about your information, message or call us on <a href={site.whatsapp}>{site.phone}</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
